WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.206 --> 00:00:02.789
(street noise)

00:00:04.223 --> 00:00:08.390
- Peter Parker, what brings
you into my office today?

00:00:09.866 --> 00:00:12.548
- Well, I don't really
know how to explain it.

00:00:12.548 --> 00:00:14.585
I got bit by this glowing, green spider,

00:00:14.585 --> 00:00:17.986
and ever since then I've felt different.

00:00:17.986 --> 00:00:19.096
- Yeah? Different how?

00:00:19.096 --> 00:00:20.152
- I feel better.

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:20.985
- Oh yeah?

00:00:20.985 --> 00:00:21.818
- Stronger.

00:00:21.818 --> 00:00:22.651
- Okay.

00:00:22.651 --> 00:00:23.484
- Faster.

00:00:23.484 --> 00:00:26.776
- [Narrator] Pete, always remember,

00:00:26.776 --> 00:00:29.311
with great power comes great--

00:00:29.311 --> 00:00:31.811
- You have radiation sickness.

00:00:35.106 --> 00:00:35.939
- I'm sorry.

00:00:35.939 --> 00:00:38.261
- I know it's hard to hear but yeah,

00:00:38.261 --> 00:00:41.332
you were bit by a glowing,
green, radioactive spider.

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:42.459
It's radiation sickness.

00:00:42.459 --> 00:00:46.525
We have to get you on
treatment immediately.

00:00:46.525 --> 00:00:48.356
- That can't be true.

00:00:48.356 --> 00:00:50.576
- It can be. I'm a doctor and it is.

00:00:50.576 --> 00:00:53.988
- Then how come after I got
bit, I felt really lightheaded.

00:00:53.988 --> 00:00:57.235
- That's literally symptom
number one of radiation sickness.

00:00:57.235 --> 00:00:58.643
- But then I passed
out and I was clenching

00:00:58.643 --> 00:01:00.276
my covers really hard.

00:01:00.276 --> 00:01:01.548
- Also a symptom.

00:01:01.548 --> 00:01:02.802
Do you think these are good things

00:01:02.802 --> 00:01:03.932
that are happening to you?

00:01:03.932 --> 00:01:06.604
- Doc, doc, listen. If I were sick,

00:01:06.604 --> 00:01:08.937
then how come I can do this?

00:01:10.339 --> 00:01:13.465
(grunts and laughs)

00:01:13.465 --> 00:01:15.706
- You just jumped a normal height,

00:01:15.706 --> 00:01:16.699
was that supposed to be impressive?

00:01:16.699 --> 00:01:17.761
- Now that I have these gifts,

00:01:17.761 --> 00:01:19.860
I feel like I should combat evil.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.388
- Peter, these delusions of
grandeur are side effects

00:01:22.388 --> 00:01:24.500
of very serious radiation sickness.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:28.128
- Delusions?! Dude, I was
just swingin' on a web,

00:01:28.128 --> 00:01:29.962
through New York City!

00:01:29.962 --> 00:01:31.962
Oh my god! I'm doing it.

00:01:33.109 --> 00:01:35.230
I'm webbing! Yes!

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:36.691
- We live in Detroit, and I just saw you

00:01:36.691 --> 00:01:38.885
get out of a cab ten minutes ago.

00:01:38.885 --> 00:01:40.717
- You know what, with these abilities,

00:01:40.717 --> 00:01:42.659
I can avenge Uncle Ben.

00:01:42.659 --> 00:01:44.059
Uncle Ben!

00:01:44.059 --> 00:01:44.892
No!

00:01:45.948 --> 00:01:47.280
- What do you mean avenge Uncle Ben?

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.520
He's fine, he was in the cab with you.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:50.983
- Goodbye Peter. Have fun at the doctor's

00:01:50.983 --> 00:01:52.841
knowing that I am very
much alive and well.

00:01:52.841 --> 00:01:53.938
- You know what?

00:01:53.938 --> 00:01:54.786
- [Doctor] Peter?

00:01:54.786 --> 00:01:55.754
I think I can do this.

00:01:55.754 --> 00:01:58.254
- [Doctor] What are you doing?

00:01:59.144 --> 00:02:00.071
Stop it.

00:02:00.071 --> 00:02:00.950
- Finally!

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:02.599
- [Doctor] Peter!

00:02:02.599 --> 00:02:04.608
- Finally, I can make a
difference in the world!

00:02:04.608 --> 00:02:06.525
- Peter, that's enough!

00:02:10.186 --> 00:02:11.524
You are very ill.

00:02:11.524 --> 00:02:13.501
We need to start an
aggressive treatment plan,

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:16.119
and we cannot do that with
you monkeying around my office

00:02:16.119 --> 00:02:19.612
like some kind of eight-legged monkey.

00:02:19.612 --> 00:02:21.229
- I knew you were gonna say that,

00:02:21.229 --> 00:02:22.629
because of my spider sense.

00:02:22.629 --> 00:02:23.677
- That's it, I'm done.

00:02:23.677 --> 00:02:25.199
You kids always come in here
with the exact same thing.

00:02:25.199 --> 00:02:26.917
- Woah, wait, woah.

00:02:26.917 --> 00:02:28.701
What do you mean, "You kids"?

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:30.196
- Do you think you're the first
teenage, aspiring reporter

00:02:30.196 --> 00:02:34.363
to come into my office with
a radioactive spider bite?

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:39.801
- Hello, Doctor.

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:40.695
- Hello.

00:02:40.695 --> 00:02:42.374
- What's all this, then?

00:02:42.374 --> 00:02:44.847
- Are all the other ones British?

00:02:44.847 --> 00:02:46.472
- Unfortunately, yeah.

00:02:46.472 --> 00:02:48.119
- Well what about that guy?

00:02:48.119 --> 00:02:49.288
- Hey Doc, I've been feeling a little--

00:02:49.288 --> 00:02:51.750
- You will never have radiation sickness.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.500
And I don't care if it is Cannon.

00:02:59.161 --> 00:03:02.411
(upbeat hip-hop music)

